WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.998 --> 00:00:18.629
The next morning Brody was eating breakfast when a hawk landed in the courtyard.

2
00:00:19.931 --> 00:00:21.892
It quickly transformed into Hermes.

3
00:00:21.912 --> 00:00:25.815
"Come, my champion," Hermes said to Brody.

4
00:00:25.835 --> 00:00:28.978
"I'm taking you to the agora to show you off."

5
00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:31.240
"Show him off?"

6
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.441
Julia said.

7
00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:36.743
"I thought we were supposed to blend in so Zeus doesn't notice Brody."

8
00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:38.824
Hermes eyed her.

9
00:00:38.844 --> 00:00:42.186
"You talk a great deal for a mortal girl.

10
00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:43.587
But you're partly correct.

11
00:00:43.987 --> 00:00:46.688
I don't want Zeus to know where I'm keeping my champion.

12
00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:49.630
Zeus might decide to tamper with him when I'm not here."

13
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.153
"Huh?" Brody looked up from his bread and fruit.

14
00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:56.974
"What do you mean, tamper with me?"

15
00:00:56.994 --> 00:00:59.996
"Never mind that.

16
00:01:00.332 --> 00:01:01.672
You're under my protection, boy."

17
00:01:02.293 --> 00:01:03.893
Hermes patted him on the shoulder.

18
00:01:03.913 --> 00:01:08.735
"I can keep you safe, and also show you off in public."

19
00:01:10.095 --> 00:01:11.836
"Okay," Julia said.

20
00:01:11.856 --> 00:01:15.917
"But listen, I've been thinking about that time passage we came through.

21
00:01:16.437 --> 00:01:18.418
It sounds like it could easily close up again.

22
00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.838
Could we end up trapped here forever?"

23
00:01:20.858 --> 00:01:24.119
"Forever?" Brody echoed.

24
00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:26.240
He didn't like the sound of that.

25
00:01:27.312 --> 00:01:31.615
Ancient Greece was pretty cool so far—he was looking forward to competing in the Games.

26
00:01:34.236 --> 00:01:37.618
But he already missed TV and video games and playing football.

27
00:01:37.638 --> 00:01:43.381
"You don't need to worry about the time passage," Hermes said.

28
00:01:43.401 --> 00:01:48.944
"Caerus assures me the passage should remain stable at least through the Games.

29
00:01:49.485 --> 00:01:51.586
After that, you're welcome to return home."

30
00:01:51.606 --> 00:01:53.887
"Do you promise?"

31
00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.328
Julia asked.

32
00:01:56.108 --> 00:01:58.049
"You'll let us go right after the Games?"

33
00:01:58.069 --> 00:02:00.010
"Of course."

34
00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:01.410
Hermes shrugged.

35
00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.611
"Now come to the agora."

36
00:02:08.553 --> 00:02:11.054
The agora was Olympia's central square.

37
00:02:12.715 --> 00:02:18.257
Dozens of merchants and farmers were there selling goods like honey, fish, silk, and gems.

38
00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:22.419
People and gods wandered around shopping and chatting.

39
00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:24.700
"Is Zeus here?"

40
00:02:25.168 --> 00:02:26.329
Julia asked Hermes.

41
00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:28.770
"I don't see him.

42
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:29.390
But look."

43
00:02:29.831 --> 00:02:31.732
Hermes pointed to someone in the distance.

44
00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:34.273
"There's his lovely wife.

45
00:02:34.893 --> 00:02:35.954
Let's go and say hello."

46
00:02:35.974 --> 00:02:38.715
"Zeus has a wife?"

47
00:02:39.316 --> 00:02:40.436
Brody asked Julia.

48
00:02:41.637 --> 00:02:43.078
She gave him a scornful look.

49
00:02:43.098 --> 00:02:46.340
"Didn't you pay attention in social studies?

50
00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.900
Zeus' wife is Hera.

51
00:02:48.261 --> 00:02:49.882
She's a very powerful goddess."

52
00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:54.144
"And a very scary one," Markos whispered.

53
00:02:54.912 --> 00:02:57.353
"Be careful not to say anything that might insult her."

54
00:02:58.414 --> 00:03:03.496
Hera was a tall, stately woman with a sharp chin and even sharper black eyes.

55
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:09.118
"Greetings, Hermes.

56
00:03:09.718 --> 00:03:11.559
Who are these young mortals?"

57
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.920
Hermes yanked Brody forward.

58
00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.422
"I'm pleased to introduce my champion for the Games.

59
00:03:18.962 --> 00:03:20.863
Say hello to the queen of the gods, Brody."

60
00:03:22.483 --> 00:03:23.724
"Hi," Brody said.

61
00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.221
"Nice to meet you."

62
00:03:25.241 --> 00:03:29.204
"Brody Hera repeated.

63
00:03:29.224 --> 00:03:31.786
"What sort of name is that?

64
00:03:32.347 --> 00:03:33.848
It doesn't sound Greek to me."

65
00:03:35.129 --> 00:03:38.311
Hermes squeezed Brody's shoulder to stop him from responding.

66
00:03:38.331 --> 00:03:43.015
"Perhaps it does not sound Greek," Hermes said quickly.

67
00:03:43.035 --> 00:03:47.599
"But as you can hear, the boy speaks Greek as well as you and I do."

68
00:03:47.619 --> 00:03:53.444
"Hmm." Hera stared at Brody, her eyes suspicious.

69
00:03:55.012 --> 00:04:00.914
"So, Hera," Hermes said innocently, "I hear Zeus has found himself another impressive champion.

70
00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:05.275
Do you know whether this mortal hero has yet arrived in Olympia?"

71
00:04:06.675 --> 00:04:07.595
Hera stiffened.

72
00:04:07.615 --> 00:04:12.477
"I have better things to do than keep track of Zeus' business."

73
00:04:12.497 --> 00:04:15.177
"Of course you do."

74
00:04:15.758 --> 00:04:16.698
Hermes smiled.

75
00:04:18.158 --> 00:04:20.899
"Still, you must be as curious as the rest of us.

76
00:04:21.439 --> 00:04:22.720
What's the fellow's name again?

77
00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:29.315
Alexandros?" "Alcides," another goddess said, walking over to join them.

78
00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:33.017
"Zeus' hero is named Alcides."

79
00:04:33.037 --> 00:04:36.120
"Greetings, Athena."

80
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.222
Hermes bowed, and Hera nodded coolly.

81
00:04:39.242 --> 00:04:44.365
"Athena?" Julia whispered, elbowing Brody.

82
00:04:44.385 --> 00:04:48.048
"Wow! She's the goddess of wisdom.

83
00:04:48.508 --> 00:04:50.309
She was always my favorite goddess."

84
00:04:50.329 --> 00:04:53.972
"You're such a nerd!"

85
00:04:54.428 --> 00:04:55.489
he said, laughing.

86
00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.932
The gods were all exchanging rumors about Alcides.

87
00:04:59.952 --> 00:05:05.836
"He's said to be the strongest mortal of his generation," Hermes told Athena.

88
00:05:05.856 --> 00:05:10.519
"It's hard to know what is true," Athena replied.

89
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.761
She sounded disapproving.

90
00:05:12.781 --> 00:05:17.704
"I'm afraid you all exaggerate your heroes' abilities so greatly.

91
00:05:19.045 --> 00:05:22.528
The Games are meant to be an honest contest," she went on.

92
00:05:23.676 --> 00:05:27.577
"Not some silly competition full of deception and cheating."

93
00:05:27.597 --> 00:05:31.698
"Don't be a spoilsport, Athena," Hermes said.

94
00:05:31.718 --> 00:05:34.599
"Our gossip and mischief are just good fun.

95
00:05:34.979 --> 00:05:38.540
And I will have even more fun when my champion defeats Zeus' hero!"

96
00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:41.001
Brody grinned.

97
00:05:41.021 --> 00:05:43.981
"Don't worry, I'll do it," he bragged.

98
00:05:45.082 --> 00:05:46.402
Hermes clapped him on the back.

99
00:05:46.422 --> 00:05:47.782
"That's the spirit, boy!"

100
00:05:49.023 --> 00:05:50.863
Hera eyed Brody with scorn.

101
00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.844
"We'll see about that.

102
00:05:54.172 --> 00:05:57.535
If you'll excuse me, I have things to do."

103
00:05:59.677 --> 00:06:00.597
She stalked off.

104
00:06:01.118 --> 00:06:02.539
Athena wandered away too.

105
00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:07.083
As soon as the goddesses were gone, two more gods rushed over.

106
00:06:08.304 --> 00:06:12.807
One was a muscular young man with wavy dark hair and mischievous golden eyes.

107
00:06:14.328 --> 00:06:18.312
The other was a pretty young woman with a bow slung over one slim shoulder.

108
00:06:19.473 --> 00:06:23.456
She had the same wild, dark hair and golden eyes as the young man.

109
00:06:24.936 --> 00:06:27.579
"Apollo, Artemis," Hermes greeted them.

110
00:06:27.599 --> 00:06:29.140
"How are you, my friends?"

111
00:06:30.741 --> 00:06:35.366
"We heard you found your champion," Artemis said, staring curiously at Brody.

112
00:06:35.386 --> 00:06:38.468
"Why, he's very impressive."

113
00:06:38.488 --> 00:06:42.532
"Thanks." Brody puffed up his chest.

114
00:06:42.552 --> 00:06:46.636
"Hera seemed impressed too," Hermes said.

115
00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:51.180
"Though I suspect she's much more concerned about Zeus' champion."

116
00:06:52.748 --> 00:06:56.729
"Ah, the mighty Alcides," Apollo said with a laugh.

117
00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:58.510
"Have you seen him yet?"

118
00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:02.451
"No one has seen him yet," Artemis said.

119
00:07:02.471 --> 00:07:09.293
"According to the rumors, Zeus is keeping him hidden in the hills until Zeus is ready to present

120
00:07:09.353 --> 00:07:11.774
him." Hermes smirked.

121
00:07:12.394 --> 00:07:13.274
"You know Zeus.

122
00:07:13.854 --> 00:07:15.455
He likes to make a dramatic entrance."

123
00:07:17.155 --> 00:07:19.136
"Yes," Apollo agreed.

124
00:07:19.956 --> 00:07:24.340
"He also must know that everyone will be looking for ways to beat him in the Games."

125
00:07:25.821 --> 00:07:26.762
Brody spoke up.

126
00:07:26.782 --> 00:07:29.104
"Don't worry, I'll beat his hero.

127
00:07:29.584 --> 00:07:33.468
I scored more touchdowns last season than anyone in the history of my middle school!"

128
00:07:34.589 --> 00:07:37.611
The gods stared at him, looking amused and puzzled.

129
00:07:38.752 --> 00:07:39.913
Then Hermes chuckled.

130
00:07:41.835 --> 00:07:43.916
"Perhaps the boy is right," he said.

131
00:07:43.936 --> 00:07:47.940
"Perhaps Zeus failed to find a suitable hero this time.

132
00:07:49.076 --> 00:07:52.319
That could be another reason Zeus is keeping Alcides hidden."

133
00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.162
"Perhaps." Artemis sounded doubtful.

134
00:07:56.182 --> 00:08:02.426
"But I won't believe it until I see you and your champion setting off on the victory tour

135
00:08:02.527 --> 00:08:04.168
of Greece after the Games."
